# API endpoints

Every backend URL the browser calls is a `VITE_*` variable, baked in at build time. Declare it in `.env.development`, `src/vite-env.d.ts`, and the Vite `server.proxy` table.

Dev values are relative paths. Vite proxies them to `http://localhost:3001`. The dev server is the API host, so paths have no `/api` prefix.

```
VITE_GRAPHQL_URL=/graphql
VITE_AUTH_REFRESH_URL=/auth/refresh
```

Production values are absolute and sit behind `/api`. The reverse proxy strips that prefix before the request reaches the Node server.

```
VITE_GRAPHQL_URL=https://trashnet.de/api/graphql
VITE_ISALIVE_URL=https://trashnet.de/api/isalive
VITE_AUTH_REFRESH_URL=https://trashnet.de/api/auth/refresh
VITE_AUTH_LOGOUT_URL=https://trashnet.de/api/auth/logout
```

A new endpoint needs both shapes. A relative production path hits the static site, not the API. After changing a `VITE_*` value, rebuild. The running bundle does not pick it up.
